{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe default test suite passes but `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py::test_install_from_sdist_preserves_commit` emits Python's `DeprecationWarning` at line 143: Python 3.14 will filter extracted tar archives by default and may reject files or modify metadata. The test calls `TarFile.extractall(extracted)` without an explicit `filter=` policy.\n\n## Reproduction\nRun the named test with warnings enabled under the repository virtualenv. The warning is deterministic on Python 3.12 and identifies the future 3.14 behavior change.\n\n## Plan\nUse rebar-debug to establish the intended safe extraction policy and prove whether the test fixture requires metadata that a standard filter changes. Apply the smallest compatibility repair with a RED warning-as-error oracle; do not weaken archive-safety behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The named build-provenance test runs with its tar extraction warning promoted to an error and passes.\n- [x] The selected extraction filter is explicit and justified against the fixture's required metadata.\n- [x] Existing build-provenance assertions remain unchanged or stronger.\n- [x] The focused test and repository gates pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786927641735567001,"uuid":"d2b46d11-c131-46ed-9020-56864ff042b8"}